  "findings": [
    "Both modes add exactly one seven-byte read hint (0f188831010000, prefetcht0 0x131(%rax)) in kd_mutex_run_combiner; parent has none at this displacement.",
    "Default-off hint: .text0x19186, combiner+0x1f6; current-body call .text0x191ce. Mode2 hint: .text0x1a19b, combiner+0x34b; current-body call .text0x1a1e6.",
    "Combiner grows7 bytes in both modes. Removing the hint yields exact normalized instruction/relocation identity, including preserved branch targets. Call counts remain17(default-off)/26(mode2); no outlined helper or added fentry.",
    "Executor hot/cold instruction counts, call counts and normalized relocation targets are preserved. The only normalized instruction changes are two +2 diagnostic source-line immediates per hot/cold function. Exact owner/PICKUP, epoch/gate, CPU/READY and key/generation probes remain.",
    "Default-off total .text remains136911 bytes; combiner growth consumes alignment space and representative function addresses remain. Mode2 .text grows64 bytes, later slowpath moves16 and later local/cold functions40hex, so binary/layout identity is not claimed.",
    "Epoch-end and owner predicate bytes/relocations are exactly unchanged in both modes; default-off waiter slowpath exact; mode2 waiter slowpath normalized instructions/relocations exact despite shifted placement.",
    "Source runtime diff is solely one prefetch statement plus its explanatory comment; all other changes are docs. Frozen worktree remains clean."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "These are captured build-gate ELFs, not a claim that any live or nano invocation used these exact bytes. Root owns live execution and its receipts.",
    "Source/ELF consistency and unchanged checks do not establish cache residency, reduced stalls, or performance improvement. Prefetch may be ignored by hardware.",
    "Existing compiler-name/percpu/objtool warnings remain in supplied logs; successful build receipts are not warning-free or mitigation-coverage proof.",
    "Module srcversion is identical across parent/candidate despite the changed private .inc code and ELF bytes; use source commit and exact ELF SHA256, not srcversion, for identity."
  ],
  "method": {
    "ELF": "Read ELF64 headers, section bytes, symbols and RELA records directly using a standalone standard-library reader; hashes cover supplied .ko bytes.",
    "disassembly": "System objdump -drw disassembles the supplied .ko as data. Function rows are bounded by the ELF symbol sizes, excluding following alignment padding.",
    "hint_comparison": "Remove only candidate instruction prefetcht0 0x131(%rax), then recompute internal instruction indices. Both modes exactly match parent normalized combiner instructions including per-instruction relocation targets.",
    "line_constants": "Executor/cold normalized differences are retained explicitly and checked against source KD_PR_DEBUG/KD_PR_ERR line constants; no blanket immediate masking.",
    "normalization": "Instruction mnemonic/operands retained. RIP comments omitted; relocated operands compare normalized target symbol/offset and relocation type/byte position within instruction. Direct internal branch targets map to instruction indices, so insertion-induced address changes do not appear as semantic changes. External direct targets retain symbol+offset."
  },
